      "knowledge_point_id": "90a5c75b-e93d-5f09-a126-3d0cb5ede2d5",
      "knowledge_point": "Writing a Factorial in an Equivalent Form",
      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $(n+3)!$ for any $n\\ge -1?$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the definition of factorial, we have\n\n$$\n(n+3)!=(n+3)\\cdot (n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1.\n$$\n\nNow, applying the factorial definition to all but the first factor, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(n+3)! & =(n+3)\\cdot \\overset{(n+2)!}{\\overset{⏞}{(n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1}} \\\\  & =(n+3)\\cdot (n+2)!\\end{aligned}\n$$",
